## Why This Is Asked

This question tests understanding of advanced scheduling techniques, concurrency primitives, and NUMA awareness under high contention scenarios.

## Key Concepts

- Per-core run queues and load distribution
- Lock-free data structures and atomic operations
- Work stealing algorithms and victim selection strategies
- Starvation avoidance and fairness mechanisms
- Memory locality considerations and memory barriers

## Code Example

```c
// Pseudo-C implementation
typedef struct Task { 
    int id; 
    struct Task *next; 
} Task;

typedef struct Deque { 
    volatile Task *head; 
    volatile Task *tail; 
} Deque;

void enqueue(int core, Task *t) { /* CAS push to tail */ }
Task* dequeue(int core) { /* CAS pop from head */ }
Task* steal(int victim_core) { /* CAS steal from tail */ }
