## Why This Is Asked
Tests practical thinking about read-ahead, IO overlap, and correctness under concurrent readers in a real OS path.

## Key Concepts
- Read-ahead triggers based on access patterns
- Window sizing and IO overlap
- Prefetch state and synchronization
- Cache invalidation and eviction

## Code Example
```c
typedef struct { int last_block; int window; int prefetched; } file_cache_t;
void on_block_access(file_cache_t *fc, int bno) {
  int stride = bno - fc->last_block;
  if (abs(stride) == 1) { /* sequential pattern */ prefetch_range(fc, bno+1, fc->window); }
  fc->last_block = bno;
}
```

